    {
      "title": "SpaceX’s Starship returns to launch pad from orbit in victory for company",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/14/spacex-starship-double-catch",
      "description": "<p>Although booster exploded, company caught upper stage for first time in campaign to make megarocket reusable</p><p>SpaceX’s megarocket Starship <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/13/spacex-starship-megarocket-blasts-off-earth-orbit\">returned</a> to its Texas launch tower on Saturday, a milestone in the company’s efforts to make the craft suitable for human spaceflight.</p><p>The 171ft (52-meter) bullet-shaped upper stage descended into the clutch of the tower’s mechanical arms, ending a 22hr mission where the craft orbited Earth 14 times.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/14/spacex-starship-double-catch\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T22:35:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX’s Starship nails a smooth return with historic catch",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/11/15/aje-onl-nf_spacexs-starship-nails-a-smooth-return-141126?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "SpaceX Starship made a triumphant return to Earth, caught midair by giant mechanical ‘chopsticks’.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-11-15T01:22:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX’s Starship captured by launchpad arms in dramatic first",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/spacexs-starship-captured-by-launchpad-arms-in-dramatic-first?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "SpaceX officials say catch by mechanical arms shows Starship&#039;s full reusability, crucial for rapid, low-cost recycling.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-11-15T00:14:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX makes first launch pad catch of Starship after its orbital return",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/spacex-makes-first-launch-pad-catch-of-starship-after-its-orbital-return-126111500023_1.html",
      "description": "SpaceX's Starship made a triumphant return to Earth on Saturday, caught in midair by giant mechanical arms where its journey began 22 hours earlier.\nIt was the grand finale that Elon Musk and his team hoped for - the first-ever capture of a Starship flying back from space. But with the first-stage booster exploding shortly after Friday's liftoff from Texas, the company fell short of its desired double catch.\nWreckage remained in the Gulf of Mexico, cordoned off by buoys, as the stainless steel, bullet-shaped spacecraft lowered itself upright at the launch pad.\nThe dramatic, sci-fi-like capture helped blot out the booster's messy miss.\n\"Can you believe it?\" shouted SpaceX commentator Dan Huot.\nSpaceX officials said Saturday's catch demonstrates the full reusability of Starship, intended for moon and Mars travel. Although Friday's booster recovery failed, the company had already made three previous booster catches, validating the technique.\nNASA welcomed Saturday's news. The space",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-15T02:18:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX successfully catches Starship rocket in huge milestone for the space industry",
      "link": "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/spacex-successfully-catches-starship-rocket-in-huge-milestone-for-the-space-industry-f42c136c?mod=mw_rss_topstories",
      "description": "The historic first gets SpaceX closer to “rapid reusability” of rockets.",
      "source_name": "MarketWatch Top Stories",
      "published": "2026-11-15T00:33:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX catches upper stage of Starship rocket in historic first",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/14/spacex-plans-to-try-first-ever-catch-of-starship-rocket-from-orbit.html",
      "description": "Starship Test Flight 15 marked the first time Elon Musk's company tried to catch both the booster and upper stage of the rocket.",
      "source_name": "CNBC Top News",
      "published": "2026-11-14T23:10:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "Watch SpaceX successfully execute the first ‘chopstick’ catch of Starship",
      "link": "https://www.theverge.com/science/1033930/spacex-chopstick-starship-catch",
      "description": "After aborting a planned catch of Starship Flight 15's booster, SpaceX successfully captured Starship with its \"Mechazilla\" launch and catch tower for the first time. The company has performed 'chopstick' catches of its boosters before, but this is the first time the maneuver has successfully been executed on the Starship vehicle itself. SpaceX CEO Elon [&#8230;]",
      "source_name": "The Verge All Posts",
      "published": "2026-11-14T21:44:44"
    },
    {
      "title": "SpaceX successfully catches Starship after launch for the first time",
      "link": "https://www.engadget.com/2316926/watch-spacex-attempt-to-catch-the-starship-upper-stage-for-the-first-time/",
      "description": "While the company has pulled off this trick a few times with Super Heavy boosters, it was a first for the Ship.",
